    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="20.2a">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:LeisWl">Leis Wl</ref> 20.2a</head>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="xno" source="#robertson" n="20.2a" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="262" ed="#robertson"/>E s'il fust desaparaillé qu'il n'oust cheval ne armes, fust quite par C sol.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="263" ed="#robertson"/>And if he was without equipment, having neither horse nor arms, it shall be discharged by the payment of 100 shillings.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="507"><ref target="clause:IICn_71-2">II Cn 71.2</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 71, 2</note>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 262–263 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text (K–M) not yet added</note>
      </div>
